   $q$How does the comparison of translating to "a coat / that fit me once" develop the poem's theme?$q$, $q$[{"text":"It reveals that the father forces the speaker to translate against the speaker's will.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"},{"text":"It suggests that the speaker is too poor to buy new clothing.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"literal-reading"},{"text":"It shows that the speaker has outgrown the need to help the family at all.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"overstates-claim"},{"text":"It shows a role that once felt like play now feels heavy and ill fitting, yet is still expected each day.","is_correct":true}]$q$::jsonb, $q$It shows a role that once felt like play now feels heavy and ill fitting, yet is still expected each day.$q$, $q$The coat image contrasts the "magic trick" of age eight with a duty that no longer fits but "still gets handed to me every morning." Reading the coat as real clothing misses the metaphor.$q$, 'draft', '03aa796a-0ab7-593c-a290-c6cc033d038e')
