   $q$Which choice is the best objective summary of the passage?$q$, $q$[{"text":"A widow calls a stream Two Kettles because her grandparents found kettles in its bank.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"too-narrow"},{"text":"While helping survey a valley, Wendell secretly records local place names; after Holt sees them, the atlas adds an appendix crediting those names.","is_correct":true},{"text":"A selfish surveyor ignores the valley's people until a clever boy shames him into changing.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"includes-opinion"},{"text":"Wendell replaces all of Holt's names with local ones, and the atlas prints only the local names.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"adds-false-detail"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$While helping survey a valley, Wendell secretly records local place names; after Holt sees them, the atlas adds an appendix crediting those names.$q$, $q$The correct choice traces the survey, the second notebook, and the appendix without judging Holt. The maps kept Holt's names, so the choice saying only local names were printed is false.$q$, 'draft', '640cdf0e-ec79-5269-8460-e6e48ea6f1a2')
