   $q$How does the contrast in the first two paragraphs help develop the theme?$q$, $q$[{"text":"It shows that the residents were confused about the geography of their own valley.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"contradicts-text"},{"text":"It shows that Holt and the residents were openly arguing about what to call each place.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"},{"text":"Names honoring officials are set against names rooted in residents' memories and daily lives, raising the question of whose knowledge counts.","is_correct":true},{"text":"It explains why the survey took so long to finish in the spring of 1884.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"off-topic"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$Names honoring officials are set against names rooted in residents' memories and daily lives, raising the question of whose knowledge counts.$q$, $q$Holt Creek and Commissioner's Ridge honor officials, while Two Kettles and the Long Shade come from flood stories and afternoon shadow. No argument between Holt and the residents occurs.$q$, 'draft', '640cdf0e-ec79-5269-8460-e6e48ea6f1a2')
