   $q$How does the final paragraph complicate the theme rather than simply resolve it?$q$, $q$[{"text":"It shows that Holt rejected the local names entirely and Wendell's effort failed.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"contradicts-text"},{"text":"It shows that Wendell became a surveyor himself and later renamed every place in the valley.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"adds-false-detail"},{"text":"It reveals that the residents disliked having their names printed in a government atlas.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"},{"text":"The local names are honored and credited, but only in an appendix, so they gain a place in the record without replacing the official ones.","is_correct":true}]$q$::jsonb, $q$The local names are honored and credited, but only in an appendix, so they gain a place in the record without replacing the official ones.$q$, $q$The atlas uses Holt's names on its maps but lists forty-two local names "in Common Use" in the appendix, a partial victory. Holt wrote the heading himself, so he did not reject the names.$q$, 'draft', '640cdf0e-ec79-5269-8460-e6e48ea6f1a2')
