   $q$How does the rockslide episode build a second theme on top of the theme of sharing knowledge?$q$, $q$[{"text":"It shows that experience is worthless once the land changes, so only youth matters.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"overstates-claim"},{"text":"It shows that old and young each hold knowledge the other lacks, so real security comes from mutual dependence.","is_correct":true},{"text":"It shows that nature is cruel and that no planning can protect anyone from danger.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"},{"text":"It shows that Teska was right to hide her knowledge, since the young argue among themselves.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"contradicts-text"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$It shows that old and young each hold knowledge the other lacks, so real security comes from mutual dependence.$q$, $q$Teska cannot climb the slope and the young cannot judge what they find, so each needs the other. Her experience is still essential to judging the places, so it is not worthless.$q$, 'draft', '14de3638-bd5a-502a-a9c5-697b5d2d8f23')
