   $q$The prefix trans- means "through" or "across," and luc means "light." What are "translucent" bodies?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Bodies that let light pass through them","is_correct":true},{"text":"Bodies that travel across the bay at night","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"ignores-second-root"},{"text":"Bodies that change color in the sunlight","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"},{"text":"Bodies that give off a bright blue glow","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"confuses-related-word"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$Bodies that let light pass through them$q$, $q$Trans plus luc means light passing through, and the passage says the bodies "let sunlight pass straight through them." Glowing blue is what the organisms do in darkness, not what translucent means.$q$, 'draft', 'e3c23a21-e91e-5e9a-bdfa-606154d2af13')
