   $q$The Greek prefix neo- means "new" or "young." Which description best fits "neoteny" as the passage uses it?$q$, $q$[{"text":"An adult keeping features normally seen only in the young","is_correct":true},{"text":"A young animal developing adult features very early","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"reverses-relationship"},{"text":"An animal that lives far longer than its relatives","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"},{"text":"A newly discovered species living in a single lake","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"too-literal"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$An adult keeping features normally seen only in the young$q$, $q$Neo- signals youth, and the passage defines neoteny as "the keeping of youthful features into adulthood," like an adult axolotl with juvenile gills. Developing adult features early reverses that direction.$q$, 'draft', '9a26d17e-2591-5be8-b3e2-5287ae4ca605')
