  ('e071c7fd-a401-5a77-aac5-4c49b386d3e2', null, (select id from public.skills where slug = 'read-g12-word-parts'), null, 'easy',
   $q$The prefix circum- means "around," and vent means "to come" or "to go." What did Adaeze choose to do when she decided to "circumvent" the slower boat?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Go around it to get past","is_correct":true},{"text":"Turn back to wait for it","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"opposite-meaning"},{"text":"Follow directly behind it","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"ignores-prefix"},{"text":"Signal it to move aside","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"context-only-guess"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$Go around it to get past$q$, $q$Circum plus vent means to go around, and the passage explains she was "slipping past on the inside." Following behind is exactly what the passage says she chose not to do ("Rather than trailing behind").$q$, 'draft', 'd0ad9405-d926-5787-b2f2-fa201e805e69')
