   $q$The Greek root pan means "all," and horama means "view." What is a "panorama" in the passage?$q$, $q$[{"text":"A painting that shows only the sky above a city","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"too-narrow"},{"text":"A painting that surrounds viewers with a view in every direction","is_correct":true},{"text":"A painting made by one artist working entirely alone","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"contradicts-text"},{"text":"A painting small enough to be carried from city to city","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"ignores-root-clues"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$A painting that surrounds viewers with a view in every direction$q$, $q$Pan plus horama means a view of all, and visitors "could turn in every direction and see one continuous scene." A painting by one artist alone contradicts the "teams of assistants" the passage describes.$q$, 'draft', '451f4af7-ccaf-5ea7-9a85-5e91edabce6e')
