   $q$The prefix con- means "together," greg means "flock" or "group," and -ate makes a verb. What did crowds do when they "congregated" at popular panoramas?$q$, $q$[{"text":"They waited separately in long lines","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"ignores-prefix"},{"text":"They gathered together in groups","is_correct":true},{"text":"They left quickly after a short look","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"opposite-meaning"},{"text":"They argued about the paintings' details","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$They gathered together in groups$q$, $q$Con plus greg means to flock together, and the crowds stayed "for hours, pointing out details to one another." Leaving quickly contradicts the hours they spent there.$q$, 'draft', '451f4af7-ccaf-5ea7-9a85-5e91edabce6e')
