   $q$The prefix tele- means "far," and metry means "measurement." What is the "telemetry" mission teams receive?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Calculations of how far the craft has traveled","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"too-narrow"},{"text":"Instructions that engineers send to the craft","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"reverses-direction"},{"text":"Measurements sent back from a distant craft","is_correct":true},{"text":"Photographs of moons taken through a telescope","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"ignores-second-root"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$Measurements sent back from a distant craft$q$, $q$Tele plus metry means measuring from far away, and the passage lists the measurements: "fuel level," "battery charge," and instrument temperature. Instructions sent to the craft reverse the direction of the information.$q$, 'draft', '522d847e-ee97-58b3-95a7-1ab8533b8011')
