   $q$The prefix ab- means "away from," and err means "to wander." Which meaning of "aberration" is best supported by the last paragraph?$q$, $q$[{"text":"A mistake made by the team in reading the numbers","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"misattributes-cause"},{"text":"A deliberate change engineers made to test the system","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"},{"text":"A lasting fault that signals a failing instrument","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"contradicts-text"},{"text":"A brief departure from the normal pattern that clears up by itself","is_correct":true}]$q$::jsonb, $q$A brief departure from the normal pattern that clears up by itself$q$, $q$An aberration wanders away from the normal, and this one "disappears on its own." The passage contrasts it with "a real fault," so a lasting failure is the opposite case, not the aberration.$q$, 'draft', '522d847e-ee97-58b3-95a7-1ab8533b8011')
