   $q$The Latin root nov means "new." What does it mean that Lucia felt like a "novice"?$q$, $q$[{"text":"She felt like a beginner with little experience","is_correct":true},{"text":"She felt like a visitor touring the museum","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"context-only-guess"},{"text":"She felt like an expert among beginners","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"opposite-meaning"},{"text":"She felt like a writer working on a novel","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"spelling-coincidence"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$She felt like a beginner with little experience$q$, $q$A novice is someone new to an activity, and the passage ends by contrasting her first day with no longer feeling "like a beginner." Being an expert reverses the meaning, since the others knew far more than she did.$q$, 'draft', '230ec808-114e-5f94-b5c8-a72e2ad58f48')
