   $q$The prefix re- means "again," nov means "new," and -ation names a process. Why was the room closing for a "renovation"?$q$, $q$[{"text":"So its animals could be returned to the wild","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"},{"text":"So it could be torn down and replaced by offices","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"overstates-meaning"},{"text":"So it could be closed to the public permanently","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"ignores-root-clues"},{"text":"So it could be repaired and made like new again","is_correct":true}]$q$::jsonb, $q$So it could be repaired and made like new again$q$, $q$Re plus nov means making new again, and the curator wants to "keep what still works and repair the rest." Tearing the room down goes beyond renewal, since he plans to keep parts of it.$q$, 'draft', '230ec808-114e-5f94-b5c8-a72e2ad58f48')
