   $q$The prefix in- means "not," anim means "life" or "spirit," and -ate means "having." What are "inanimate" creatures?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Creatures that move in a lifelike way","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"ignores-prefix"},{"text":"Creatures that are not alive","is_correct":true},{"text":"Creatures that come from inside the valley","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"misreads-prefix"},{"text":"Creatures that are very rare or endangered","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"context-only-guess"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$Creatures that are not alive$q$, $q$In plus anim means without life, and the passage confirms the animals "were perfectly still." They only seemed lifelike because of skillful posing, which is why the moving choice is tempting but wrong; reading in- as "inside" is also a mistake here.$q$, 'draft', '230ec808-114e-5f94-b5c8-a72e2ad58f48')
