   $q$The Latin root belli means "war," and the suffix -ose means "full of." What does it mean that blue jays are more "bellicose" than chickadees?$q$, $q$[{"text":"They are larger and heavier birds","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"context-only-guess"},{"text":"They are louder and more musical singers","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"too-narrow"},{"text":"They are shyer and more cautious","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"opposite-meaning"},{"text":"They are more aggressive and ready to fight","is_correct":true}]$q$::jsonb, $q$They are more aggressive and ready to fight$q$, $q$Belli plus ose means warlike, and the jays "chase smaller birds away." Their "loud calls" are part of the description, but loudness alone misses the fighting sense of the root.$q$, 'draft', '0d56c0a4-d8a4-525e-bc7d-64be0afa701d')
