   $q$Which sentence best fills the blank in sentence (2) to state the opinion?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Walking means moving from place to place on your feet.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"definition-not-opinion"},{"text":"Brookside School is three blocks away from the town park.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"fact-not-opinion"},{"text":"Some students at our school ride the bus every morning.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"fact-not-opinion"},{"text":"Our school should hold a Walk to School Day once a month.","is_correct":true}]$q$::jsonb, $q$Our school should hold a Walk to School Day once a month.$q$, $q$The correct choice tells what the writer thinks the school should do, and sentences (3) through (8) support it. The other choices are facts or a definition that the reasons do not support.$q$, 'draft', '3862fa9f-bc08-52ed-9899-dd7cd3ebb5b9')
