        '3-5', $q$My First Clay Cup$q$, $q$(1) On Saturday morning, my aunt Rosalind took me to a pottery studio for my first lesson. (2) The room smelled like wet earth, and shelves of drying bowls lined every wall. (3) The teacher, Mr. Okafor, showed me how to press a lump of clay onto the center of the wheel. (4) I pushed the pedal, and the wheel began to spin. (5) My clay wobbled and fell to one side. (6) Clay is a kind of soil made of tiny bits of rock. (7) I tried again, but the clay slid off the wheel and landed with a splat. (8) "Keep your elbows on your knees," Mr. Okafor said. "Hold your hands still and let the wheel do the work."

(9) I took a deep breath and tucked my elbows in tight. (10) The clay rose slowly between my fingers like a tiny tower. (11) I pressed my thumbs into the top and opened it into a small cup.

(12) Then we cleaned up.$q$, 'draft')
