        '3-5', $q$Where Is Pepper?$q$, $q$(1) On a windy Tuesday afternoon, our neighbor Mrs. Delgado knocked on our door. (2) Her orange cat, Pepper, had slipped outside while she carried in the groceries. (3) My brother Theo and I promised to help her look. (4) We checked under the porch, behind the recycling bins, and inside the empty flowerpots. (5) Theo shook a bag of cat treats while I called Pepper's name. (6) We searched for a long time.

(7) Then I heard a tiny meow coming from above our heads. (8) Pepper was sitting on a high branch of the maple tree, looking very proud of herself. (9) Theo ran home for the step ladder, and Dad came out to hold it steady. (10) I climbed up three steps and held out a treat. (11) Pepper sniffed it, then crept down into my arms.

(12) Mrs. Delgado hugged Pepper tightly. (13) That is what happened.$q$, 'draft')
