  ('62b0a454-a6b1-5d07-967f-3b376d20a271', null, (select id from public.skills where slug = 'write-g5-narrative-writing'), null, 'hard',
   $q$The writer wants to add a sentence between sentences 7 and 8 to slow down the most exciting moment. Which sentence does this best?$q$, $q$[{"text":"I froze, tipped my head back, and searched the leaves until I spotted a flash of orange.","is_correct":true},{"text":"Earlier that morning, I had eaten oatmeal for breakfast.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"breaks-sequence"},{"text":"Cats can hear many sounds that people cannot hear.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"off-topic-fact"},{"text":"Then we found Pepper and took her home.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"rushes-pacing"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$I froze, tipped my head back, and searched the leaves until I spotted a flash of orange.$q$, $q$Breaking the moment into small actions (freezing, looking up, spotting orange) slows the pacing right when the reader wants to know where the meow came from. "Then we found Pepper and took her home" speeds past the exciting part instead of slowing it down.$q$, 'draft', '9486b3b9-edfe-54a1-8296-3bc1ac50b348')
