-- Passage wg5-narrative-writing-p03
insert into public.passages (id, code, skill_id, sat_alignment, grade_band, title, body, status)
values ('7f47078a-3e1b-5a9a-b377-48ed0abd9c51', 'wg5-narrative-writing-p03', (select id from public.skills where slug = 'write-g5-narrative-writing'), null,
        '3-5', $q$A Bite Out of the Sun$q$, $q$(1) On the morning of the partial solar eclipse, Grandpa Hiroshi and I made a pinhole viewer from a cereal box. (2) We cut a small square in one end and taped foil over it. (3) Then Grandpa poked a tiny hole in the foil with a pin. (4) "Never look straight at the sun," he reminded me. "We will watch its light on the paper instead." (5) At noon, we carried the box out to the backyard. (6) I stood with my back to the sun and peeked through the viewing hole.

(7) At first, I saw only a small white circle on the paper inside. (8) I thought the eclipse was boring. (9) Slowly, a dark bite appeared on one edge of the circle. (10) The bite grew bigger and bigger until the sun looked like a glowing crescent moon. (11) The air turned cooler, and the birds in the hedge grew quiet. (12) Our neighbor has a blue car.

(13) After about an hour, the bite shrank away, and the circle was whole again. (14) I put the viewer on my shelf.$q$, 'draft')
